        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor(mac): make app node a CLI capability superset",
        "body": "Closes #105568\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a problem where the macOS app maintained a second node-host implementation and could expose fewer or different capabilities than `openclaw node`. The app and CLI could also appear as separate Gateway nodes instead of one Mac node with the full capability union.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe macOS app remains the sole Gateway node identity and keeps native/TCC-sensitive commands in the signed app. A private JSONL worker now runs the canonical TypeScript node-host runtime for CLI-owned system, filesystem, browser/plugin, skills, and MCP capabilities; shell execution still crosses the app-owned authenticated exec-host socket. Duplicate Swift browser, filesystem, and system execution paths are removed.\n\nRemote onboarding also installs the CLI without starting an unrelated local Gateway, and debug source builds now prefer their checkout CLI over a stale global install.\n\n## User Impact\n\nMac users get one node whose capability set is a superset of the CLI node plus native Mac capabilities. TCC-sensitive execution remains in the signed app context, while CLI and Mac App behavior share one runtime implementation.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `pnpm test src/node-host/worker.test.ts src/node-host/runner.test.ts src/node-host/invoke.test.ts src/node-host/invoke-system-run.test.ts src/cli/command-startup-policy.test.ts src/cli/command-path-policy.test.ts` — 138 tests passed.\n- `swift test --package-path apps/macos --filter 'MacNodeHostWorkerTests|MacNodeModeCoordinatorTests|OnboardingViewSmokeTests|UpdateOrchestrationTests'` — 65 tests passed.\n- `swift test --package-path apps/shared/OpenClawKit --filter GatewayNodeSessionTests` — 55 tests passed.\n- `swift test --package-path apps/macos --filter CommandResolverTests` — 26 tests passed.\n- Signed debug app built and launched from this branch. Gateway showed one approved Mac node with 10 capabilities and 15 commands spanning native canvas/screen plus CLI browser, file, MCP, system, and session surfaces.\n- Live `system.which` invocation succeeded through the shared worker. Live native `screen.snapshot` reached the app and failed closed because Screen Recording permission is disabled on the test Mac.\n- Fresh structured autoreview: no accepted/actionable findings.\n",
